1
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,410
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:35,570
Lucky!

37
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:38,820
I'm so lucky that I can go shopping
with you today, Mr. Kaji!

38
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:43,370
What?! Isn't this the swimsuit section?

39
00:01:39,870 --> 00:01:43,370
<i><i>Please allow us to announce
a call for a customer.</i></i>

40
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:44,410
Hey! Hey! How do you like this?

41
00:01:43,370 --> 00:01:48,580
<i><i>Mr. Yamazaki from lbaragi City,
your friend is waiting for you.</i></i>

42
00:01:44,410 --> 00:01:48,580
Slow down, school girl.
Aren't you a little young for that?

43
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:52,800
<i><i>Please come to Customer Service
on the first floor.</i></i>

44
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:50,960
You're just so behind the times, Mr. Kaji.

45
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:53,050
This is pretty normal nowadays.

46
00:01:54,010 --> 00:01:56,470
Really? I had no idea.

47
00:01:56,470 --> 00:02:00,800
But this is the big school trip.
You've got to go all out!

48
00:02:00,550 --> 00:02:01,970
Travel Pamphlet
Public Middle School 1

49
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:02,260
And where are you going for the trip?

50
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:04,520
Activity Destinations

51
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:04,520
Day 1 - Depart from New Tokyo-3 International Airport to Okinawa (New Kadena, Main Island)

52
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:04,520
Day 2 - Main Island to Kerama Islands to Miyako Island

53
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:04,520
Day 3 - Miyako Island to Arrive at New Tokyo-3 International Airport

54
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:04,520
Okinawa!

55
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:07,730
We're even scheduled to go scuba diving!

56
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:09,560
Schedule

57
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:09,560
Day 2

58
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:09,560
Wake up

59
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:09,560
Breakfast
(buffet)

60
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:09,560
Scuba Diving
(first time)

61
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:09,560
Lunch
(boxed)

62
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:09,560
Scuba Diving
(second time)

63
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:09,940
Scuba diving...

64
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:12,820
Come to think of it, it's been
three years since I've gone diving.

65
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:16,190
Say, where did you go for your school trip?

66
00:02:16,190 --> 00:02:18,860
Oh, we didn't have one.

67
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:21,030
Why not?

68
00:02:21,030 --> 00:02:22,990
Because of the Second Impact.

69
00:02:23,030 --> 00:02:26,000
EPISODE 10
MAGMA DIVER

70
00:02:31,170 --> 00:02:33,960
I can't go on the trip?!

71
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:35,210
Right.

72
00:02:35,210 --> 00:02:36,340
Why not?!

73
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:37,590
Because you're on standby for combat duty.

74
00:02:37,590 --> 00:02:39,260
You never told me anything about that!

75
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:40,470
I just told you.

76
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:41,970
Who in the hell decided that?!

77
00:02:41,970 --> 00:02:44,720
Me, the Operations Planning Manager.

78
00:02:48,430 --> 00:02:53,360
Hey, why don't you stop slurping that tea
and say something!

79
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:54,770
You're a man, aren't you?

80
00:02:54,770 --> 00:02:58,570
Actually, I kind of anticipated
it would be like this.

81
00:02:58,570 --> 00:03:00,200
And you've already given up?

82
00:03:02,070 --> 00:03:06,040
How pathetic. Nothing's more useless
than a housebroken male.

83
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:08,370
Please don't talk about me like that.

84
00:03:08,710 --> 00:03:10,830
I know how you must feel,

85
00:03:10,830 --> 00:03:12,880
but there's just no helping this.

86
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:17,760
There's always the possibility of
an Angel attack while you're gone.

87
00:03:18,260 --> 00:03:21,880
It's always standby!
Standby, standby, standby!

88
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:25,430
We've always got to be ready to defend
against an enemy who may not even come!

89
00:03:25,430 --> 00:03:28,730
Why don't you try to find out where they are,
and attack them for once?!

90
00:03:29,310 --> 00:03:31,980
If we could do that,
we'd have already done it.

91
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:35,520
Look, think of this as a good opportunity.

92
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:38,190
While the rest of your class is on the trip,

93
00:03:38,190 --> 00:03:40,570
the two of you can study a little.

94
00:03:40,570 --> 00:03:42,780
Or do you think I don't know about these?

95
00:03:43,950 --> 00:03:47,160
You're greatly mistaken if you thought
I wouldn't find out about these.

96
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:53,080
What you get on your tests at school
is piped directly to me.

97
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:56,790
It's ridiculous. Who cares about grades?

98
00:03:56,790 --> 00:04:00,340
I've got absolutely no interest in
the old-fashioned grading system.

99
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:02,930
When in Rome, do as the Romans do.

100
00:04:02,930 --> 00:04:05,260
Try to adjust to Japanese school life.

101
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:07,970
No way!

102
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:13,350
Asuka, I'll bring you some souvenirs!

103
00:04:13,730 --> 00:04:16,730
Well, it's just too bad for you guys!

104
00:04:16,730 --> 00:04:19,480
I'll have enough fun for both of ya!

105
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:27,660
Paste the observation data on Mt. Asama

106
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:31,040
from Balthasar to Melchior
as soon as possible.

107
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:40,130
A school trip?

108
00:04:40,130 --> 00:04:42,550
That's pretty carefree for times like these.

109
00:04:42,550 --> 00:04:44,180
Well, it's because the times are so hard

110
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:47,260
that they want to have a little fun
while they can.

111
00:04:55,690 --> 00:04:57,230
What are you up to?

112
00:04:57,650 --> 00:04:59,190
Studying science.

113
00:04:59,190 --> 00:05:01,780
You're such a diligent student.

114
00:05:01,780 --> 00:05:04,860
You can say that, but I have to do it anyway.

115
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:07,110
Ta da!

116
00:05:07,110 --> 00:05:10,620
Since I can't go scuba diving in Okinawa,
I'm going to do it here!

117
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:12,040
Really?

118
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:14,250
Let's see. What're you working on?

119
00:05:14,250 --> 00:05:15,580
Let me take a look.

120
00:05:16,540 --> 00:05:19,340
You can't solve an easy equation like this?

121
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:21,750
There, done.

122
00:05:21,750 --> 00:05:23,630
It's so easy.

123
00:05:23,630 --> 00:05:25,840
How can you solve a difficult
problem like this,

124
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:27,890
and not make good grades on your tests?

125
00:05:28,390 --> 00:05:31,760
Because I couldn't figure out
what the questions said.

126
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:34,930
You mean you couldn't read
the questions in Japanese?

127
00:05:34,930 --> 00:05:38,020
Right, I haven't learned all
the Chinese characters yet.

128
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:40,400
We didn't study it in college over there.

129
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,270
College?

130
00:05:41,270 --> 00:05:43,780
Oh, I graduated last year.

131
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:46,780
So, what does this one say?

132
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:49,320
It's about thermal expansion.

133
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:53,040
Thermal expansion? That's kid stuff!

134
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:54,290
To put it simply,

135
00:05:54,290 --> 00:06:00,080
things expand when they get hot,
and shrink when they get cold.

136
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:02,250
Well, yeah, but...

137
00:06:02,250 --> 00:06:06,720
If I were to warm up just my breasts,
do you think they'd grow a little bigger?

138
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:09,680
I wouldn't know anything about that!

139
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:11,640
What a boring guy.

140
00:06:31,910 --> 00:06:34,120
Watch this, Shinji!

141
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:36,910
Back roll entry!

142
00:06:51,090 --> 00:06:53,140
This just isn't clear enough.

143
00:06:53,140 --> 00:06:56,100
But just as the report from Mt. Asama
Earthquake Research Laboratory says,

144
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:57,730
this shadow is definitely suspicious.

145
00:06:57,730 --> 00:06:59,940
Of course, we can't ignore this.

146
00:06:59,940 --> 00:07:01,690
What is the Magi's judgment?

147
00:07:01,690 --> 00:07:03,480
Fifty-fifty.

148
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:04,570
Is someone there yet?

149
00:07:04,570 --> 00:07:07,150
Captain Katsuragi's already on site.

150
00:07:12,530 --> 00:07:13,870
You're too deep!

151
00:07:13,870 --> 00:07:15,830
Not yet. Another 500, please.

152
00:07:21,870 --> 00:07:25,630
Depth 1200. The pressure resistant
partition is cracking.

153
00:07:25,630 --> 00:07:27,170
Ms. Katsuragi!

154
00:07:27,170 --> 00:07:29,760
If it breaks, we'll pay for the damage.
200 more.

155
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:35,100
We're monitoring a reaction!

156
00:07:37,140 --> 00:07:38,270
Begin analysis!

157
00:07:38,270 --> 00:07:38,600
Yes, Ma'am!

158
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:50,860
The probe has imploded due
to the extreme pressure.

159
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:51,950
What about the analysis?

160
00:07:51,950 --> 00:07:55,410
Just barely made it. The pattern is blue.

161
00:07:55,410 --> 00:07:58,620
There's no doubt, it's an Angel.

162
00:07:58,620 --> 00:08:01,210
As of now, this laboratory will be
completely sealed off!

163
00:08:01,210 --> 00:08:03,330
It's under Nerv's jurisdiction now!

164
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:05,500
Any and all access to the outside
world is prohibited,

165
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:08,920
and all records of the events of the
past six hours are classified.

166
00:08:10,380 --> 00:08:14,840
Seismic Wave Analysis Room 2

167
00:08:10,380 --> 00:08:14,840
Seismic Wave Analysis Room 1

168
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:15,050
Request an A-17 from Commander lkari,
top priority!

169
00:08:15,050 --> 00:08:18,430
Watch what you're saying.
This is an open line.

170
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:22,520
I know. Hurry up and switch
to a scrambled line.

171
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:24,270
A-17?!

172
00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:25,860
We're going to launch an offensive?

173
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:27,230
Correct.

174
00:08:27,230 --> 00:08:29,280
Unacceptable, it's too dangerous.

175
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:31,900
You had better not say you've forgotten
what happened fifteen years ago.

176
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:36,240
This is a chance to move from
a consistently defensive posture

177
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:38,450
to an offensive one for the first time.

178
00:08:38,450 --> 00:08:40,660
The risk is too large.

179
00:08:40,660 --> 00:08:46,580
However, I'm sure you're aware how
important a live Angel sample would be.

180
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:48,920
We will not tolerate failure.

181
00:08:50,420 --> 00:08:52,210
Failure?

182
00:08:52,210 --> 00:08:55,430
If we fail, it will result in the extinction
of the human race.

183
00:08:56,260 --> 00:08:58,600
You're really sure about this?

184
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:01,180
This is an Angel?

185
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:05,690
Yes, it's something like a chrysalis
prior to reaching the adult stage.

186
00:09:05,690 --> 00:09:09,270
This operation's prime objective
is to capture this Angel.

187
00:09:09,270 --> 00:09:12,820
We must capture it alive, as close
to its original state as possible.

188
00:09:12,820 --> 00:09:14,070
And if we can't?

189
00:09:14,070 --> 00:09:16,280
Then you must destroy it immediately.
Do you understand?

190
00:09:16,280 --> 00:09:16,910
Yes, Ma'am!

191
00:09:16,910 --> 00:09:18,530
The designated pilot for
the actual operation is...

192
00:09:18,530 --> 00:09:21,290
Hey, let me! I'll dive!

193
00:09:21,290 --> 00:09:23,790
But I'll bet it's going to be me again.

194
00:09:23,790 --> 00:09:25,710
Asuka.

195
00:09:25,710 --> 00:09:27,370
Carry out the mission using Unit 02.

196
00:09:27,370 --> 00:09:30,670
Sure! This'll be a piece of cake.

197
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:31,880
And me?

198
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:36,180
The prototype Unit 00 isn't compatible with
the special equipment we'll be using.

199
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:39,100
Rei and Unit 00 will remain at
headquarters on standby.

200
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:40,010
Yes, Ma'am.

201
00:09:40,010 --> 00:09:41,720
Oh, too bad for you.

202
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:43,140
You don't get to go to the hot springs.

203
00:09:44,850 --> 00:09:47,980
Since an A-17 has been ordered,
we'll scramble immediately.

204
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:48,980
Get ready.

205
00:09:48,980 --> 00:09:49,520
Yes, Ma'am!

206
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:57,490
You say this is the heat resistant plug suit,
but it's not any different.

207
00:09:57,490 --> 00:09:59,160
Try pressing the switch on the right.

208
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:02,660
Oh, no!

209
00:10:02,990 --> 00:10:05,160
What is this?!

210
00:10:05,580 --> 00:10:07,620
Unit 02 is also ready.

211
00:10:08,040 --> 00:10:12,250
No! What is that?!

212
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:15,710
The suit is designed to protect you from
heat, pressure, and radiation.

213
00:10:15,710 --> 00:10:18,340
This is Type-D equipment, for combat
under extreme environmental duress.

214
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:21,390
Is that my Unit 02?

215
00:10:22,470 --> 00:10:24,850
No way! Count me out!

216
00:10:24,850 --> 00:10:27,430
I don't want to appear in public in this!

217
00:10:27,430 --> 00:10:29,940
This sort of thing is up Shinji's alley!

218
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:31,940
That's too bad.

219
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:34,690
I was anticipating seeing Asuka's
gallant figure!

220
00:10:34,690 --> 00:10:36,530
No!

221
00:10:37,530 --> 00:10:41,990
But I don't have the courage to go
in front of Mr. Kaji looking so uncool!

222
00:10:41,990 --> 00:10:43,160
This is a problem.

223
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:45,290
Yes...

224
00:10:45,290 --> 00:10:47,290
Excuse me, but I...

225
00:10:47,290 --> 00:10:48,790
I'll go in Unit 02.

226
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:54,920
Sorry, but I don't want you
touching my Unit 02!

227
00:10:55,710 --> 00:10:58,380
I'd rather do it than let
the First take my place.

228
00:11:00,890 --> 00:11:03,430
I know it's uncool, but put up with it, okay?

229
00:11:15,940 --> 00:11:19,320
Eva Units 01 and 02 have arrived.

230
00:11:19,650 --> 00:11:22,030
Have both units stand by in position.

231
00:11:22,030 --> 00:11:24,830
Move in the laser bore, and ready the crane.

232
00:11:24,830 --> 00:11:25,620
Roger.

233
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:26,830
Boom arm fixed in place.

234
00:11:26,830 --> 00:11:29,040
Coolant circulation system going on auto.

235
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:31,620
Hey, where's Mr. Kaji?

236
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:34,500
That jerk won't be here.
There's nothing for him to do.

237
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:38,710
Damn! I wanted him to see how great I am.

238
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:41,130
So, an A-17 has been ordered.

239
00:11:41,130 --> 00:11:44,140
That includes the freeze of all current assets.

240
00:11:44,140 --> 00:11:47,180
I'm sure there are many people who
will be put out by that.

241
00:11:47,180 --> 00:11:48,970
Why didn't you stop them?

242
00:11:48,970 --> 00:11:52,900
I didn't have any excuse.
The order was official.

243
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:56,730
But if Nerv fails, it'll mean
the end of the world.

244
00:11:56,730 --> 00:11:59,490
They're not that arrogant.

245
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:04,200
What are those?

246
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:06,870
The UN's Air Force is on standby alert.

247
00:12:06,870 --> 00:12:08,740
Until this mission has been completed.

248
00:12:08,740 --> 00:12:10,500
Are they going to help us?

249
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:12,540
No, they're here to clean up.

250
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:14,380
In case we fail.

251
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:16,500
What do you mean?

252
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:20,380
They will use N2 depth charges to
destroy the Angel, and us with it.

253
00:12:20,710 --> 00:12:22,090
That's awful!

254
00:12:22,090 --> 00:12:24,590
Who would order something like that?

255
00:12:24,590 --> 00:12:26,180
Commander Ikari.

256
00:12:32,270 --> 00:12:34,230
Laser operation, complete.

257
00:12:34,230 --> 00:12:35,440
The bore path has been secured.

258
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:37,820
The Type D equipment
is functioning normally.

259
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:40,030
Unit 02 is in position to dispatch.

260
00:12:40,230 --> 00:12:41,740
Roger.

261
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:43,570
Asuka, are you ready?

262
00:12:43,570 --> 00:12:45,110
Anytime you are.

263
00:12:45,110 --> 00:12:45,950
Launch!

264
00:12:55,790 --> 00:12:57,500
Looks hot!

265
00:13:00,590 --> 00:13:02,970
Unit 02 is entering the lava.

266
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:04,970
Watch this, Shinji!

267
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:08,390
Giant stroke entry!

268
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:17,770
Current depth, 170. Speed of descent, 20.

269
00:13:17,770 --> 00:13:19,150
No problems detected.

270
00:13:19,150 --> 00:13:22,530
Visibility is zero. I can't see a thing.

271
00:13:22,530 --> 00:13:24,530
Switching to CT monitor.

272
00:13:27,110 --> 00:13:29,450
Even with this, visibility is no more than 120.

273
00:13:32,830 --> 00:13:35,040
Depth, 400...

274
00:13:35,040 --> 00:13:36,870
450...

275
00:13:36,870 --> 00:13:38,250
500...

276
00:13:38,250 --> 00:13:39,960
550...

277
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:41,170
600...

278
00:13:41,170 --> 00:13:42,340
650...

279
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:49,800
900...

280
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,640
950...

281
00:13:51,640 --> 00:13:52,770
1000...

282
00:13:52,770 --> 00:13:54,100
1020...

283
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:55,980
We're over the maximum safe depth.

284
00:13:56,850 --> 00:14:00,360
Depth is 1300. Estimated target level.

285
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:02,230
Asuka, can you see anything?

286
00:14:02,610 --> 00:14:05,070
No reactions detected. It's not here.

287
00:14:05,070 --> 00:14:07,570
It seems the lava current
is faster than we thought.

288
00:14:07,570 --> 00:14:10,450
The target's velocity doesn't
match our predictions.

289
00:14:10,450 --> 00:14:11,990
Hurry up and re-calculate.

290
00:14:11,990 --> 00:14:14,910
Continue the operation. Resume descent.

291
00:14:20,250 --> 00:14:22,590
Depth, 1350...

292
00:14:22,590 --> 00:14:24,170
1400...

293
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:27,340
A crack has occurred in
the second coolant pipe.

294
00:14:27,340 --> 00:14:29,590
Depth, 1480...

295
00:14:29,590 --> 00:14:31,850
We're over the maximum allowed depth.

296
00:14:31,850 --> 00:14:34,560
We haven't made contact with the target yet.

297
00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:35,810
Keep going.

298
00:14:35,810 --> 00:14:36,850
How's it going, Asuka?

299
00:14:36,850 --> 00:14:40,440
Looks like we're still good. I just want to
hurry up, finish this, and take a shower.

300
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:43,360
There's a nice hot spring near here.
We'll hit it once we're done.

301
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,900
Hang in there a little longer.

302
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:50,490
Maximum allowed depth plus 120.

303
00:14:52,700 --> 00:14:55,290
Eva Unit 02 has lost its prog knife.

304
00:14:55,290 --> 00:14:57,370
Maximum allowed depth plus 200.

305
00:14:57,370 --> 00:14:59,790
Miss Katsuragi, any more than this and...

306
00:14:59,790 --> 00:15:02,290
There's a human on board this time!

307
00:15:02,290 --> 00:15:04,960
I am in charge of this operation.

308
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:05,920
Proceed, please.

309
00:15:07,130 --> 00:15:10,590
Misato's right. I'm okay. I can keep going.

310
00:15:15,970 --> 00:15:18,480
Depth, 1780...

311
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:20,480
We've reached the adjusted target depth.

312
00:15:24,060 --> 00:15:24,900
There it is!

313
00:15:28,530 --> 00:15:30,700
Visual confirmation of the target.

314
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:31,780
Prepare to capture.

315
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:36,580
Both of you are being moved
by convection currents,

316
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:39,330
so you'll only have one chance
to make contact.

317
00:15:39,330 --> 00:15:41,460
I know. Leave it to me.

318
00:15:41,460 --> 00:15:43,750
T-minus 30 to contact.

319
00:15:43,750 --> 00:15:46,840
Relative velocity 2.2. I'm now on the axis.

320
00:15:52,550 --> 00:15:54,760
Electromagnetic cage deployed.
No problems detected.

321
00:15:55,220 --> 00:15:56,970
The target has been captured.

322
00:15:58,520 --> 00:15:59,770
Nice one, Asuka.

323
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:04,270
Capture operation completed.

324
00:16:04,270 --> 00:16:05,690
I'm coming up now.

325
00:16:11,110 --> 00:16:12,700
Are you all right, Asuka?

326
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:16,370
Of course! Fear is often worse
than the danger, as they say.

327
00:16:16,370 --> 00:16:17,990
It really was a piece of cake.

328
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:22,500
But this is more of a sauna suit
than a plug suit.

329
00:16:23,170 --> 00:16:26,000
I can't wait to get to the hot spring.

330
00:16:26,710 --> 00:16:29,380
Looks like the tension let loose all at once.

331
00:16:29,380 --> 00:16:30,260
You think?

332
00:16:30,260 --> 00:16:33,550
You were scared about this operation too,
weren't you?

333
00:16:33,550 --> 00:16:37,430
Well, yeah, because if we handled it badly,
we'd have had a repeat performance.

334
00:16:37,430 --> 00:16:39,930
That's true, the Second Impact.

335
00:16:40,220 --> 00:16:41,890
We don't need another of those.

336
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:45,310
What's going on?!

337
00:16:49,730 --> 00:16:52,360
Not good! It's started to emerge!

338
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:54,070
It's much earlier than we predicted!

339
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:55,110
Status of the cage?!

340
00:16:55,110 --> 00:16:56,530
No way it can hold!

341
00:16:59,830 --> 00:17:02,250
Abort the capture! Jettison the cage!

342
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:06,830
We're changing the operation!

343
00:17:06,830 --> 00:17:09,000
Destroying the Angel is now top priority!

344
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:12,090
Unit 02, prepare for combat as you withdraw!

345
00:17:12,090 --> 00:17:13,130
What I've been waiting for!

346
00:17:17,590 --> 00:17:20,600
Damn, I forgot I dropped the knife!

347
00:17:21,350 --> 00:17:22,270
It's right in front!

348
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:24,940
Releasing ballast!

349
00:17:28,310 --> 00:17:29,150
It's fast!

350
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:35,700
This is bad. I've lost sight of it.

351
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:38,660
In addition to that, I've got lousy visibility,
I'm really hot,

352
00:17:38,660 --> 00:17:40,950
and this suit's plastered to me
and feels disgusting.

353
00:17:40,950 --> 00:17:42,540
This really sucks.

354
00:17:42,540 --> 00:17:44,160
Asuka!

355
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:47,750
We'll take this chance to drop you
Unit 01's knife. Catch it!

356
00:17:47,750 --> 00:17:49,420
Roger!

357
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:52,420
Oh, no! Have you dropped it yet, Shinji?

358
00:17:56,340 --> 00:17:58,890
Contact with knife, 40 seconds.

359
00:17:58,890 --> 00:18:00,600
The Angel is approaching rapidly!

360
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:03,310
No! Go away!

361
00:18:03,310 --> 00:18:05,890
Hurry up with it!

362
00:18:05,890 --> 00:18:08,900
Come on, it's too slow!

363
00:18:17,150 --> 00:18:18,280
Oh, no!

364
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:25,410
Unbelievable! How could it open its mouth
in such an environment?

365
00:18:25,410 --> 00:18:27,120
Its construction must be incredible!

366
00:18:32,170 --> 00:18:33,590
Left leg damaged!

367
00:18:33,590 --> 00:18:34,500
Engage heat shields!

368
00:18:36,130 --> 00:18:38,550
Damn you!

369
00:18:42,550 --> 00:18:46,810
If it can withstand such a high heat,
high pressure environment,

370
00:18:46,810 --> 00:18:48,190
then the prog knife will be useless against it!

371
00:18:48,190 --> 00:18:49,770
Then what should we do?

372
00:18:49,770 --> 00:18:50,600
I know!

373
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:51,860
Just like earlier!

374
00:18:52,810 --> 00:18:54,650
Eat this!

375
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:58,610
I see! Thermal expansion!

376
00:18:58,610 --> 00:19:02,120
Transfer all coolant pressure
to cable three! Hurry!

377
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:31,940
Right when I succeeded...

378
00:19:33,360 --> 00:19:35,730
Oh, man, is this it?

379
00:19:47,040 --> 00:19:48,290
Shinji?

380
00:19:52,170 --> 00:19:54,710
Idiot, don't go overboard.

381
00:19:58,170 --> 00:20:03,090
Oomiya

382
00:20:01,550 --> 00:20:03,550
Hello?

383
00:20:03,090 --> 00:20:08,010
Welcome
Nerv
Party

384
00:20:03,550 --> 00:20:06,300
Is there anyone from Nerv here?

385
00:20:06,300 --> 00:20:08,010
Yes!

386
00:20:08,970 --> 00:20:11,730
I need your signature here.

387
00:20:12,730 --> 00:20:15,190
Thanks so much.

388
00:20:15,190 --> 00:20:16,650
From Mr. Kaji?

389
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:18,650
What could it be?

390
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:24,570
The bath is over there, to the left.

391
00:20:29,450 --> 00:20:31,580
Heavenly!

392
00:20:35,380 --> 00:20:39,090
I never knew a bath could feel this good.

393
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:42,220
Shinji, can you hear me?

394
00:20:42,220 --> 00:20:43,760
Yes, Ma'am!

395
00:20:43,760 --> 00:20:45,890
Would you throw me the body shampoo?

396
00:20:45,890 --> 00:20:48,220
We ran out of ours.

397
00:20:50,640 --> 00:20:51,600
Here it comes.

398
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:53,190
Roger.

399
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:56,520
Ouch!

400
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:59,150
You idiot! Watch where you're throwing!
You suck!

401
00:20:59,150 --> 00:21:00,780
Sorry.

402
00:21:00,780 --> 00:21:03,320
Don't hit me in some weird spot.

403
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:04,910
Let me take a look.

404
00:21:05,910 --> 00:21:10,740
Wow, your skin is so soft and smooth, Asuka!

405
00:21:10,740 --> 00:21:12,870
Don't! You're tickling me!

406
00:21:12,870 --> 00:21:14,460
How about right here?

407
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:16,960
Don't touch that!

408
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:19,090
Come on, it doesn't wear out!

409
00:21:22,840 --> 00:21:25,090
It expanded.

410
00:21:25,090 --> 00:21:26,720
How embarrassing!

411
00:21:36,020 --> 00:21:39,770
Oh, this? I got this in the Second Impact.

412
00:21:43,740 --> 00:21:46,990
You know all about my past, don't you?

413
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:49,660
Well, yeah. It's part of my job.

414
00:21:50,240 --> 00:21:53,330
It's all ancient history for both of us.

415
00:21:53,330 --> 00:21:55,000
We shouldn't let it bother us.

416
00:21:57,620 --> 00:22:00,590
TO BE CONTINUED

417
00:23:06,070 --> 00:23:06,990
PREVIEW

418
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:12,410
Those who don't think well of Nerv cut off
the power supply to all of New Tokyo-3.

419
00:23:12,410 --> 00:23:15,950
With none of the modern facilities
operational, an Angel closes in.

420
00:23:15,950 --> 00:23:18,580
Next episode: "In the Still Darkness"

421
00:23:17,870 --> 00:23:21,040
IN THE STILL DARKNESS

422
00:23:18,580 --> 00:23:21,000
Expect more fan service next time too!
